---
---

<div data-reveal="out">
  <section
    aria-labelledby="questions-before-you-start"
    class="px-6 py-24 md:py-32"
  >
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[840px]">
      <p class="mb-4 text-center font-mono text-[12px] leading-none tracking-[0.18em] text-text-accent uppercase">
        FAQ
      </p>
      <h2
        id="questions-before-you-start"
        class="text-center text-[32px] leading-[1.15] font-medium tracking-[-0.03em] text-text-primary md:text-[40px]"
      >
        Questions <span class="text-gradient-heading">before you start</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-12 divide-y divide-border-default border-y border-border-default">
        <details class="group">
          <summary class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 py-5 text-[17px] font-semibold text-text-primary focus-visible:shadow-ring focus-visible:outline-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            When do I commit to anything?
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="text-[22px] leading-none font-normal text-text-accent transition-transform duration-200 ease-standard group-open:rotate-45 motion-reduce:transition-none"
            >
              +
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="max-w-[64ch] pb-6 text-[16px] leading-7 text-text-secondary">
            When you approve the role and the terms. Everything before that,
            including the written role, is free and yours to keep.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="group">
          <summary class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 py-5 text-[17px] font-semibold text-text-primary focus-visible:shadow-ring focus-visible:outline-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            Who manages the specialist day to day?
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="text-[22px] leading-none font-normal text-text-accent transition-transform duration-200 ease-standard group-open:rotate-45 motion-reduce:transition-none"
            >
              +
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="max-w-[64ch] pb-6 text-[16px] leading-7 text-text-secondary">
            You do. They work inside your team, on your priorities. We stay with
            the engagement and check in along the way.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="group">
          <summary class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 py-5 text-[17px] font-semibold text-text-primary focus-visible:shadow-ring focus-visible:outline-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            Do I have to get on a call?
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="text-[22px] leading-none font-normal text-text-accent transition-transform duration-200 ease-standard group-open:rotate-45 motion-reduce:transition-none"
            >
              +
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="max-w-[64ch] pb-6 text-[16px] leading-7 text-text-secondary">
            Only if you want to. The chat covers everything we need. The call is
            there if you’d rather talk it through with someone.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="group">
          <summary class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 py-5 text-[17px] font-semibold text-text-primary focus-visible:shadow-ring focus-visible:outline-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            Why don’t I see profiles right away?
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="text-[22px] leading-none font-normal text-text-accent transition-transform duration-200 ease-standard group-open:rotate-45 motion-reduce:transition-none"
            >
              +
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="max-w-[64ch] pb-6 text-[16px] leading-7 text-text-secondary">
            Because we introduce people who fit your role and have already said
            yes to it. You see their scores and the evidence before you meet
            them.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="group">
          <summary class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 py-5 text-[17px] font-semibold text-text-primary focus-visible:shadow-ring focus-visible:outline-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            What if the role is hard to describe?
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="text-[22px] leading-none font-normal text-text-accent transition-transform duration-200 ease-standard group-open:rotate-45 motion-reduce:transition-none"
            >
              +
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="max-w-[64ch] pb-6 text-[16px] leading-7 text-text-secondary">
            That’s what the chat is for. Start with what you know, even if it’s
            one line, and it will ask the questions that fill in the rest.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
